  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Saturday) \nIssued at 859 PM CDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nThe start of the long term will offer much of the same as ridging\nremains anchored over the TN Valley and high pressure sets up along\nthe eastern seaboard. With high pressure both at the surface and\naloft, dry and hot conditions will prevail with highs soaring into\nthe 90s each afternoon. ESE flow off the Atlantic will keep dew\npoints in the high 60s to low 70s. This will push heat indices near\nand above triple digits with heat being the primary concern through\nthe long term forecast. Make sure to continue to practice proper heat\nand sun safety. \n\nBy Friday, models begin to diverge as the ridging over the SE looks \nto retrograde. A weak front looks to approach from the NW however \nsignificant disagreement exits in the models regarded if and when \nthis front could come through. As such, ensemble spread increases in \nFriday and significantly on Saturday regarding our high temperatures,\nnearly nearly a ten degree spread widely shown in the models. Should\nthe front near by the end of the week, this would increase cloud \ncover and rain chances, and decrease temperatures. If the front \nstalls to our NE, hot and humid conditions will prevail through \nSaturday. Please check back for updates.",
